                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8058266d-6428-3bd7-9dc9-6d0f7ec79193",
                        "entry_id": "47739b56-aca3-36aa-bda7-fd0a41f7b1d1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In German literature and modern folklore, a malicious elf or spirit who preys on children."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "European"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2bc105a4-8b1e-4cb4-acee-c98b808ff427",
                                "sense_id": "8058266d-6428-3bd7-9dc9-6d0f7ec79193",
                                "text": "This line, and indeed the whole passage (lines 653-664), allude to the well-known poem by Goethe about the erlking, hoary enchanter of the elf-haunted alderwood, who falls in love with the delicate little boy of a belated traveler."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "44d3d8c4-2bac-49f6-b558-aee9216f2657",
                                "sense_id": "8058266d-6428-3bd7-9dc9-6d0f7ec79193",
                                "text": "So easy for one young son to be swallowed up in a world teeming with Erlkings, real and imagined."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "caad71ed-dfcd-462e-9249-a11263946c7c",
                                "sense_id": "8058266d-6428-3bd7-9dc9-6d0f7ec79193",
                                "text": "He was in the forest looking to see the trees / But none were there / He found a girl / She found the erlking"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7faef6f2-52ea-4a8a-bea8-434deb924b10",
                                "sense_id": "8058266d-6428-3bd7-9dc9-6d0f7ec79193",
                                "text": "By now, he seems less a cartoon character than some contemporary Erlking, the malicious spirit made famous by Goethe (and Schubert) but found originally in a Danish ballad."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
